"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/NoteheadText-swift.struct":{"title":"MXLNote.NoteheadText","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoteheadText","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NoteheadText","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/NoteheadText-swift.struct","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/noteheadtext-swift.struct","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The notehead-text type represents text that is displayed inside a notehead, as is done in some educational"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"music. It is not needed for the numbers used in tablature or jianpu notation. The presence of a TAB or jianpu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clefs is sufficient to indicate that numbers are used. The display-text and accidental-text elements allow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display of fully formatted text and accidentals."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/NoteheadText-swift.struct/Item":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/noteheadtext-swift.struct\/item","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/NoteheadText-swift.struct\/Item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for NoteheadText."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"title":"MXLNote.NoteheadText.Item"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/NoteheadText-swift.struct/init(items:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/NoteheadText-swift.struct\/init(items:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"items"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV12NoteheadTextV4ItemO","text":"Item"},{"kind":"text","text":"])"}],"title":"init(items:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLNote.NoteheadText"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/noteheadtext-swift.struct\/init(items:)"}}}